        "original_id": "462dce35-f7bc-5bd7-9937-e9377913e28c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Castle Hill, Monticello, Albemarle County, Virginia, Charlottesville, Southwest Mountains, Paris\n- People: Thomas Jefferson, Alfred Landon Rives\n- Roles: President, engineer\n- Organizations: Virginia Landmarks Register, National Register of Historic Places\n- Topics: plantations, historic properties\n\nFacts:\n- Thomas Jefferson was the third President of the United States.\n- Thomas Jefferson inherited land from his father and began designing and building Monticello at age 26.\n- Castle Hill is a historic, privately owned 600-acre plantation at the foot of the Southwest Mountains in Albemarle County, Virginia, near Monticello and Charlottesville.\n- Castle Hill is recognized by the Virginia Landmarks Register and the National Register of Historic Places.\n- Alfred Landon Rives was born on March 25, 1830, in Paris, France.\n- Alfred Landon Rives was an American engineer.\n- Alfred Landon Rives died on February 27, 1903, at Castle Hill, Virginia.",
